The algebra is correct: n+3 | n²+51 ⟺ n+3 | 60. The divisors of 60 greater than 3 are 4, 5, 6, 10, 12, 20, 30, 60 (8 divisors), giving n values 1, 2, 3, 7, 9, 17, 27, 57.

Check the sum: (4+5+6+10+12+20+30+60) − 3·8 = 147 − 24 = 123. Adding directly: 1+2+3+7+9+17+27+57 = 123. ✓

